    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d491-a2">

                <pb facs="0536" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg516"/>

                <head>No. 2.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 11, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your communication, No. 64, is received,
                    also the sum of one thousand ($1,000) dollars from the Japanese government for
                    the George Horton indemnification, which will be loaned by me at 12 per centum
                    per annum, less the advances made by me for the last six months.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE S. FISHER, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">U. S. Minister Resident in Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
